        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat: add portable table presentation blocks",
        "body": "Closes #12602\n\nAI-assisted: Codex. A clean full-patch autoreview is included in the evidence below; no session transcript is attached.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nAgents, plugins, and CLI callers can express charts and controls through portable message presentation, but structured tabular results still require Markdown or Slack-private Block Kit payloads. That makes typed values, native Slack sorting/filtering, accessibility text, and cross-channel degradation inconsistent.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdd one portable `table` presentation block with an atomic caption/headers/rows contract, then render it as Slack's current `data_table` block when the complete message fits Slack's published envelope. Non-native and unsupported paths use deterministic text-only fallback; Markdown pipe tables are deliberately not auto-promoted, and no separate report abstraction is introduced.\n\nSlack rendering preserves numeric cells as `raw_number`, enforces row/column/aggregate limits, carries complete accessible text, escapes structured values so they cannot activate mentions, retries `invalid_blocks` safely, chunks oversized sends and slash responses, and rejects oversized edits rather than dropping rows. Feishu renders table rows in cards; Telegram and other channels retain the portable fallback.\n\n## User Impact\n\nAgents can now send structured table results through the message tool, CLI, and plugin SDK. Slack users get native tables when supported and complete ordered text otherwise; screen readers, notifications, session mirrors, and clients without native support receive the same data without silent truncation.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Exact rebased-head Slack regressions: Crabbox `run_903084752a30` — 238/238 passed across regular replies, slash replies, direct actions, media, native/fallback blocks, escaping, chunking, and edit limits.\n- Exact rebased-head changed gate: Crabbox `run_a34445d7f890` — production/test typechecks, extension lint, dependency guards, database-first guard, sidecar guard, and import-cycle check passed.\n- Broad feature gate before final review fixes: Crabbox `run_e55df7e09a2c` — full `pnpm check:changed` passed.\n- Mandatory local autoreview: clean, no accepted/actionable findings; overall verdict `patch is correct`.\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n- API contract: [Slack `data_table` block reference](https://docs.slack.dev/reference/block-kit/blocks/data-table-block/).\n- Live Slack posting was not performed because no test workspace/channel destination was approved; transport behavior is covered with exact Slack Web API payload and retry tests.\n",
